From b1dafeea92d0672caae7e7088fa55d2b08c8605a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <hunter.hough@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 14:55:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] chore(scripts): add update-beads-hooks.sh + make target

Walks ~/.* and ~/code/* for every .beads/ directory and runs
`bd hooks install --beads --force` in its enclosing repo. Skips worktrees
(they share core.hooksPath with the main repo) and dirs outside a git
repo. Useful after a bd binary upgrade to refresh per-repo shim version
strings and re-assert hook presence across the machine.

  make update-hooks            - do it (53 repos updated on hammer)
  make update-hooks-dry-run    - show what would be done

Note: the fix that motivated this (beads-p4v) lives in the bd binary;
shims dispatch to `bd hooks run`, so the binary upgrade is what carries
new behavior. This target re-asserts shim presence, nothing more.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
